  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * @brief Dot product of Q15 vectors.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcA points to the first input vector
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcB points to the second input vector
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * @param[in]       blockSize number of samples in each vector
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * @param[out]      *result output result returned here
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * @return none.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  *
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * \par
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * The intermediate multiplications are in 1.15 x 1.15 = 2.30 format and these
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * results are added to a 64-bit accumulator in 34.30 format.
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * Nonsaturating additions are used and given that there are 33 guard bits in the accumulator
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * there is no risk of overflow.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  * The return result is in 34.30 format.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c ****  */
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q15.c **** 
